  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The quantitative mechanism is coherent under Q7, but Q7 does not expressly settle every domain and representative convention. Adjudication therefore separates verified declaration meaning from unresolved source applicability.",
      "primary_evidence": "The attached §1.2 paragraph describes normalized averages and edge-flux evolution. Q7 selects conditional error propagation. D002 and D011 separately impose global rectangle conservation and an integer-indexed interval grid."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation accurately reconstructs the target's substantive mathematical content. Its unresolved correspondence questions concern the source comparison domain, rather than a demonstrated mistranslation.",
      "primary_evidence": "The direct and anonymized target types have matching binders, conjunctions, error terms, and bound quantifiers; D001–D012 supply the operators reconstructed in the translation."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined. Correctness of the conditional estimate does not establish equivalence of applicability, and no genuine stronger classification follows from additional hypotheses.",
      "primary_evidence": "The methodology excludes restricted applicability from faithful-stronger. Q7 selects error accounting but does not specify an all-real-time solution requirement."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined on independently inspected evidence. Agreement between judges is not the reason for this outcome.",
      "primary_evidence": "The attached page leaves the exact discrete formula and analytic domain unstated; the supplied target fixes these through D002, D009, and D011."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D002 unclear",
      "resolution": "Declaration meaning is resolved: D002 requires locally integrable spatial slices at every real time, locally integrable temporal physical-flux slices at every spatial point, and balance for every oriented real rectangle. This is not global integrability over the entire real line. Whether its global domain and every-face representative requirement preserve source applicability remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 explicitly quantifies ∀ a b t, ∀ x s t, and ∀ a b s t. Its integrability predicates apply to finite intervals. The attached page references (1.10) without displaying it."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D003 unclear",
      "resolution": "The grid semantics are resolved through its constructor. The cells form a positive-width adjacent interval chain. Their half-open regions partition their union, so absence of an explicit domain field is not itself a demonstrated partition defect. Coverage of an independently specified physical domain is not asserted.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003 together with D004, D005, and D011 supplies L_i<R_i and R_(i−1)=L_i. These imply strictly increasing consecutive endpoints and disjoint half-open cells."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D011 unclear",
      "resolution": "The constructor imposes positivity and adjacency only. It neither requires uniform widths nor exhaustion of the real line. Integer indexing is a concrete representation whose full source applicability remains unsettled.",
      "primary_evidence": "D011 has exactly two endpoint functions and the premises ∀ i, L_i<R_i and ∀ i, R_(i−1)=L_i; no coverage, boundary, or uniformity field occurs."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C01 unclear",
      "resolution": "The selected §1.2 paragraph is confirmed from the attached image. The inherited equation (1.10) cannot be independently inspected in this tools-forbidden session, so the inherited-context portion remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 5 visibly references (1.10) in the preceding paragraph and in §1.2, but its equation display is absent."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "All target binders have definite meanings. Fin m → Real represents a positive finite real state vector, while space and time are both Real and cell indices are Int. The source correspondence of the global time domain and grid representation remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fully explicit target type quantifies m with 0<m, q : Real → Real → Fin m → Real, and grid : OneDimensionalFiniteVolumeGrid. The attached paragraph does not specify their full domains."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Positive volume, positive duration, and integrability on the actual averaging intervals are justified requirements for the selected normalized quantities. Requiring balance and slice integrability everywhere in real space and time is stronger than the local requirements of this one-step calculation; its source justification remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001, D006, D011, and hst exclude degenerate averages. D002 supplies substantially more rectangles and slices than the target uses for a fixed cell and time interval."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target is an explicit one-dimensional realization. It cannot be labeled stronger merely because it proves a quantitative consequence on that realization. Q7 authorizes the error interpretation but does not explicitly identify the full admissible solution and grid class.",
      "primary_evidence": "Q7 specifies independent old-average and time-averaged physical-flux error bounds. D002 and D011 fix additional domain structure not specified in that choice."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Normalization exceptional cases are resolved. Face representatives remain a substantive applicability issue: changing q on a fixed spatial line can leave all spatial averages unchanged while changing its temporal face flux. D002 excludes representatives that violate rectangle balance, but the supplied source page does not specify this representative convention.",
      "primary_evidence": "D010 integrates flux(q(L_j,τ)) over time. For scalar flux f(u)=u²/2 and a stationary jump from 1 to −1 at x=0, assigning q(0,τ)=0 changes the face flux from 1/2 to 0 and violates D002 on rectangles with an endpoint at 0, despite leaving spatial integrals unchanged."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target makes no unsupported existence or uniqueness claim. Its global solution premise is an applicability condition, not an existence conclusion. Whether intended forward-time solutions can be represented without extra assumptions remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "hq is an input to the target, and no existential solution binder appears in its conclusion. D002 nevertheless requires conservation at negative as well as positive times."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C01 unclear",
      "resolution": "The source location is verified visually; the missing inherited equation remains unavailable. The source contract supports the extraction but cannot replace inspection of the absent equation.",
      "primary_evidence": "The attached image shows §1.2 and §1.2.1 on printed page 5. Neither section displays (1.10)."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation correctly identifies the target's types and domains. No binder mistranslation is found; correspondence of the full domain with the interpreted source remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind target and translation both quantify positive finite state dimension, a grid over Int, q over Real × Real, arbitrary rule and old arrays, and s<t."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translated hypotheses match D002 and D011. Local analytic prerequisites are appropriate, but the selected convention does not establish that their global packaging is harmless for every source case.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translation's three conservation hypotheses reproduce D002's two slice-integrability clauses and rectangle identity. Q7 does not mention global extension."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C09 unclear",
      "resolution": "Signs, offsets, and coefficients are resolved for the stated conservative realization. Adjacency identifies face i+1 with the right boundary; conservation gives h_i(Q_i(t)−Q_i(s))=Δt(G_i−G_(i+1)). Subtracting this from the numerical update gives exactly the displayed error identity. These formulas are not explicit assertions of the selected printed paragraph.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002, D006, D009, D010, D011, and D012 yield the stated balance and scaling directly. The target's final coefficient is Δt/h_i, with both factors positive."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "Noncoverage of the entire real line is not inherently a failure because the cells partition their union and the result is local. However, equivalence to all intended physical-domain and boundary cases is not established by the supplied evidence.",
      "primary_evidence": "D011 gives an adjacent interval chain without an independently specified domain. The source says to subdivide the domain but does not identify that domain in the selected paragraph."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Half-open integration conventions do not alter cell averages under ordinary length measure. They do not resolve the separate issue of evaluating a physical flux along a fixed face. D002 enforces compatibility for admitted representatives, while completeness of representation remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "D063 and D110 define half-open oriented integration. D010 evaluates a fixed spatial point throughout a time interval. The native supplement identifies real volume with ordinary interval length."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "No well-posedness theorem is smuggled into the conclusions. The unresolved question is whether requiring an everywhere rectangle-conservative representative reduces the intended source applicability.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target concludes average certificates, identities, and a conditional norm bound, with no existence or uniqueness conclusion. D002 is an antecedent."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Under recorded Q7, the Lean conclusion supplies the selected conditional error mechanism on its represented domain. Full implication remains unclear because coverage of the interpreted source's solution and grid cases is not established.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target preserves numerical versus exact quantities and all three independent error premises. D002's global domain is not selected explicitly by Q7 or the attached paragraph."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "Under recorded Q7 and the target's explicit rectangle-conservative realization, every target conclusion is mathematically justified by normalization, conservative balance, and the norm triangle inequality. Full source-to-target correspondence remains unclear because the source plus Q7 does not completely specify that realization.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001–D012 determine the averages and update. The attached §1.2 paragraph states neither the rectangle predicate nor the discrete formula; Q7 selects conditional error propagation without fixing all domains."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation has the same scope limitation as the Lean proposition. Under Q7 it recovers the requested mechanism for admitted data, but cannot establish coverage of unrepresented source cases.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translation explicitly records the all-real-time conservation hypothesis, integer grid, and pointwise physical face evaluations; these agree with the direct declaration evidence."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The reconstructed formula and conditional bound follow within the explicit realization, but the available source and Q7 do not settle equivalence of that realization with the complete selected claim. Retain unclear rather than treating mathematical derivability under added premises as source equivalence.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translation's weighted identity follows from D002 and D009. Q7 authorizes independent error bounds but does not prescribe all-real-time existence, a representative convention, or the complete grid domain."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation, the target preserves normalized cell averages, numerical flux dependence on the old array, time-averaged physical reference fluxes, and conditional next-step error control. It is nonvacuous and supplies this mechanism for its admitted data. However, neither the attached source page nor Q7 establishes that every intended source solution and grid can be represented by the all-real-time, every-rectangle predicate and integer interval chain. The absence of a whole-line coverage field is not itself a defect, but global solution extension and face-representative applicability remain unresolved. Consequently the complete implication cannot be confirmed."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation and the explicit target realization, the conclusions follow from ordinary normalized integration and conservative balance: h_i(Q_i(t)−Q_i(s))=Δt(G_i−G_(i+1)), followed by subtraction from the numerical update and the triangle inequality. The measure supplement supports the required interval-length normalization. This verifies the quantitative calculation without inspecting the target proof. It does not establish that the source plus Q7 fixes the complete realization, including its global solution domain and pointwise face representatives. Equation (1.10) is referenced but absent from the permitted image. Full source-to-Lean correspondence therefore remains unclear."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The precise inherited statement and assumptions of equation (1.10) are not visible in the attached source image; tools are forbidden, so the supplied PDF path cannot resolve this within the present session.",
    "Q7 does not explicitly settle whether the selected comparison domain is restricted to solutions represented on all real times with conservation on every rectangle.",
    "The supplied evidence does not establish that all intended discontinuous source solutions admit the pointwise face representatives required by D002 and D010.",
    "The full relationship between the integer interval-chain representation and intended physical-domain boundary cases is not specified by the source paragraph or Q7."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-effective-domain",
      "evidence": "D002 requires slice integrability and conservation for every real spacetime rectangle. The attached §1.2 paragraph references integral conservation but does not display its inherited equation or specify all-real-time solutions. Q7 selects conditional error accounting without specifying this extension.",
      "impact": "The target may reduce applicability beyond the selected interpretation. This cannot be counted as genuine strengthening or silently treated as equivalent."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-face-representative-coverage",
      "evidence": "D010 uses temporal integrals of flux(q(L_j,τ)). Spatial-null modifications along a fixed face can change these integrals; D002 then rejects incompatible representatives. The attached source emphasizes discontinuities but supplies no representative or trace convention.",
      "impact": "The definition is coherent for admitted representatives, but coverage of the intended discontinuous source solutions remains unverified."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "verified-conservative-error-accounting",
      "evidence": "D011 identifies right(i) with left(i+1). D002 and normalized averages give exact cell balance. D009 then yields h_i e_new=h_i e_old+Δt(e_left−e_right), and positive scaling with the triangle inequality yields the stated bound.",
      "impact": "No sign, coefficient, indexing, or exact-versus-numerical substitution defect is found in the conditional calculation under Q7. The bound remains an interpretation-qualified mathematical development, not a quantitative theorem printed in the selected paragraph."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuity-and-normalization",
      "evidence": "Choose m=1, L_i=i, R_i=i+1, s=0, t=1, q=0, flux=0, old=0, and rule(s,t,old)(j)=j. D002 and D011 hold, while the update is −1 in every cell. Taking the bounds to be the actual finite error norms satisfies the conditional premises. The native volume supplement gives volume(Ioc(a,b))=ENNReal.ofReal(b−a).",
      "impact": "The theorem is not sustained solely by impossible premises, empty states, zero denominators, or zero errors. Nonvacuity does not resolve the outstanding source-domain correspondence."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "grid-partition-objection-narrowed",
      "evidence": "D011 implies consecutive strictly increasing endpoints. The half-open cell intervals are pairwise disjoint and cover their union, although they need not exhaust Real.",
      "impact": "Missing whole-line coverage is not independently sufficient for rejection. The remaining grid question concerns the intended comparison domain and boundary cases."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "I inspected the attached primary-source page and the supplied declaration, dependency, translation, judgment, and native-environment evidence without tools or independent hash recomputation. The disputed dependencies have definite mathematical meanings, and the target's normalization, conservative error identity, conditional estimate, and nonvacuity can be checked directly from their statements and definitions. The blind translation preserves those meanings. The unresolved issue is source applicability under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation: Q7 resolves the qualitative accuracy convention but does not expressly resolve global time extension, every-face representatives, or complete physical-domain coverage. The missing inherited source display cannot be replaced by a declaration name, provenance hash, or agreement between judges. Both full correspondence implications therefore remain unclear, consistently yielding undetermined and accepted=false."
}
